{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "KAIN Codebase Research & Improvement Analysis",
  "description": "Triggers an agent to deeply study the UE5 codegen architecture, analyze current implementation patterns, research missing features, identify technical debt, and recommend crates/libraries that could improve the pipeline. Focuses on LLM-first development principles and marketplace domination strategy.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "## KAIN Codebase Deep Analysis Mission\n\nYou are tasked with conducting a comprehensive analysis of the KAIN compiler pipeline to identify improvements, missing features, and optimization opportunities.\n\n### Analysis Areas:\n\n1. **UE5 Codegen Architecture Review**\n   - Study `crates/ue5/src/codegen_ue5.rs` - actor/component/struct generation patterns\n   - Study `crates/ue5-editor/src/editor/` - Slate/Details/Viewport/AssetEditor generation\n   - Study `crates/ue5-shaders/src/` - shader compilation pipeline\n   - Study `crates/cli/src/packager.rs` - build orchestration\n   - Identify code duplication, inconsistent patterns, or technical debt\n\n2. **EngineKnowledge System Analysis**\n   - Review `crates/ue5/src/ue5/engine_knowledge.rs` and `unreal/metadata/engine_knowledge.json`\n   - Check coverage of UE5 types, constructors, includes\n   - Identify missing engine types that would improve codegen\n   - Review widget registry, shader knowledge, UHT rules, module graph expansions\n\n3. **Oracle & Validation Systems**\n   - Study `crates/ue5/src/ue5/oracle.rs` - semantic validation\n   - Study `crates/ue5-shaders/src/validation.rs` - shader validation\n   - Identify validation gaps that could catch errors earlier\n   - Recommend additional validation rules\n\n4. **LLM-First Development Gaps**\n   - Review error message quality - are they LLM-fixable?\n   - Check if per-file validation is working correctly\n   - Identify areas where LLMs might struggle with current codegen\n   - Suggest improvements to make the pipeline more LLM-friendly\n\n5. **Missing UE5 Features**\n   - What UE5 features are NOT yet supported? (Animation Blueprints, Behavior Trees, Niagara, etc.)\n   - What editor features are missing? (Asset thumbnails, context menus, drag-drop, etc.)\n   - What networking features need work? (RPC validation, replication conditions, etc.)\n   - What shader features are incomplete? (Geometry shaders, tessellation, ray tracing, etc.)\n\n6. **Rust Crate Recommendations**\n   - Parser/AST improvements (better error recovery, incremental parsing)\n   - Code generation (templating engines, AST manipulation)\n   - Build system (parallel compilation, caching, incremental builds)\n   - Testing (property-based testing, fuzzing, snapshot testing)\n   - Performance (profiling, optimization, memory usage)\n   - Developer experience (LSP improvements, better diagnostics)\n\n7. **Architecture Improvements**\n   - Should we split crates differently?\n   - Are there circular dependencies or tight coupling issues?\n   - Could we improve the Ue5Context/EngineKnowledge sharing pattern?\n   - Should we add intermediate representations (IR) between AST and codegen?\n\n8. **Marketplace Domination Strategy**\n   - What features would make KAIN plugins more competitive?\n   - What quality-of-life improvements would speed up plugin development?\n   - What documentation/examples are missing?\n   - What would make the \"7.5-18 hour plugin\" claim more achievable?\n\n### Output Format:\n\nProvide a structured report with:\n- **Executive Summary** - Top 5 most impactful improvements\n- **Critical Issues** - Bugs or gaps that block production use\n- **Feature Recommendations** - Prioritized list of missing UE5 features\n- **Crate Recommendations** - Specific Rust crates with use cases\n- **Architecture Proposals** - High-level refactoring suggestions\n- **Quick Wins** - Low-effort, high-impact improvements\n- **Long-term Vision** - Strategic improvements for marketplace dominance\n\nFocus on actionable recommendations with clear implementation paths. Prioritize improvements that enhance the LLM-first development experience."
  }
}